import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'stairs':('Emergency unknown scroll read on a doorway','A wounded level-1 Warrior on an open doorway reads an unknown scroll to survive a summoner. The scroll is a Rune of Protection and the doorway cannot hold one, so the game reports no clear floor. The tracker count goes below zero; the next glyph creation then writes before the start of the arrays.'),
 'clear-floor':('Control: the same read on open floor','The same emergency read happens on ordinary floor. The rune is created, no failure message exists, and the count stays in bounds in both versions. The logs are identical before and after the fix.'),
 'pairing':('Control: ordinary tracked creation','Without any emergency, the defense chooser reads a known Rune of Protection on clear floor. The creation is tracked normally in both versions and the native grid is warded.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw}
  for tag,key in (('TRACK phaseA','phaseA'),('TRACK phaseB_acted','phaseB'),('MESSAGE','message'),('OUTCOME','outcome')):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r' (.*)',raw)
   entry[key]={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',match[1])} if match else None
  entry['decision']=[l for l in raw.splitlines() if l.startswith(('DECISION','ENGINE'))]
  entry['passed']='native-c/CBUG-0102 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw
  entry['crash']='AddressSanitizer' in raw and 'heap-buffer-overflow' in raw and 'WRITE of size' in raw
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>A failed glyph no longer drives the tracker below zero</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native emergency read, real failure message and later glyph creation</p><h1>The glyph tracker count can go below zero</h1><p>A dying low-level Warrior reads an unknown scroll while standing on a doorway. The scroll is a Rune of Protection; a doorway cannot hold one, and the game really reports that there is no clear floor. The Borg handler for that message removes a glyph that was never tracked, so the count becomes -1. The next time the Borg commands a rune creation, the guarded writer stores the position at index -1: four bytes in front of the two tracking arrays.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><br><button data-step="0">Emergency read</button><button data-step="1">Tracker after the message</button><button data-step="2">Next glyph creation</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the controls establish</h2><p>The same emergency read on ordinary floor creates the rune with no failure message; the logs are byte-identical before and after the correction. An ordinary tracked creation from a known scroll also stays identical. Only the failed read changes: the corrected handler leaves an empty tracker empty, and the later creation is stored at index 0.</p><details><summary>Memory error evidence</summary><p>Under AddressSanitizer the original aborts inside the glyph creation choice in borg-fight-defend.c with a heap-buffer-overflow WRITE before the array of size 4 at offset -4 bytes before a tracking array; the corrected build runs the same scenario cleanly. Without the sanitizer the same run is observable through the tracker count: -1 after the message and 0 after the creation instead of 0 and 1.</p></details><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Warrior level 1, depth 5, seed 1000, wounded to 8 HP, lit constructed arena, one awake mage summoner adjacent, a torch with fuel, one unidentified Rune of Protection scroll; a second, identified one is carried after the emergency read (flavor awareness is per kind). The production caution and defense routines choose; the actual requested inventory letters are validated and the reads execute through the native scroll command. The failure message is produced by the game and parsed through the real terminal scrape path.</p><p>This isolates the tracker count transition and the guarded creation write, not full autonomous play, monster AI casting or world timing. No crash claim is made for every configuration; the sanitizer abort is the recorded memory error.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/118">CBUG-0102 / issue118</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;let step=1;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);p.querySelector('.num').textContent=step===0?'Reading the unknown scroll':step===1?`Tracker count: ${d.phaseA?d.phaseA.num:'n/a'}`:`Tracker count: ${d.phaseB?d.phaseB.num:'n/a'}`;p.querySelector('.state').textContent=step===0?(d.message?`Failed-floor messages seen: ${d.message.failed_floor}.`:'No emergency read in this control.'):(step===1?(d.phaseA?(d.phaseA.num<0?'The original removed a glyph that was never tracked.':'Nothing tracked, nothing removed.'):'No emergency read in this control.'):`Native warded grid: ${d.outcome?d.outcome.glyph_created:0}.`);p.querySelector('.action').textContent=d.crash?'AddressSanitizer aborted the creation: heap-buffer-overflow write before the array.':step===2?(d.phaseB?`Creation stored the position at index ${d.phaseB.num-1}.`:'Creation never completed.'):'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='stairs'?'The original stores a creation at index -1 (four bytes before the arrays); the correction stores it at index 0. Controls unchanged.':'Both versions behave identically in this control; the logs match byte for byte.';for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.classList.toggle('active',Number(b.dataset.step)===step)}select.addEventListener('change',()=>{step=1;draw()});for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Number(b.dataset.step);draw()});draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
